{
  "blockers": [
    "Public switches 37 and 38 ('WOW' Targets, Top Targets) are printed normally-closed opto interrupters that pinned PinMAME's cvGameData inverted-switch mask does not normalize (bits 6-7 of the mask's column-3 entry are clear, unlike bits 0-5 for 31-36). This is a polarity conflict, not a spatial gap -- every dimension this report audits is complete and validated -- but it is recorded as conflict.wow-top-targets-opto-not-normalized and keeps the machine record partial until a LibPinMAME harness trace against a legal cv_20h or cv_14 ROM observes the true idle public state of 37/38."
  ],
